SINA_SMART["physics1-circulation"] = {"lecture":"physics1-circulation","title":"Biophysics of the blood circulation","mapStatus":"auto: generated by universal.py from the lecture summary and key points; not human-reviewed","los":[{"id":"physics1-circulation:e0","text":"Circulation: heart (pump), blood (fluid), vessels (closed conduits).","topic":"The big picture","sec":0,"importance":"core","highYield":"insufficient-source"},{"id":"physics1-circulation:e1","text":"Right heart: pulmonary circulation; left heart: systemic.","topic":"The big picture","sec":0,"importance":"core","highYield":"insufficient-source"},{"id":"physics1-circulation:e2","text":"Blood is non-Newtonian.","topic":"Blood and flow laws","sec":1,"importance":"core","highYield":"insufficient-source"},{"id":"physics1-circulation:e3","text":"Poiseuille: Q = πr⁴ΔP/(8ηL); ↑ viscosity → ↑ pressure (hypertension).","topic":"Blood and flow laws","sec":1,"importance":"core","highYield":"insufficient-source"},{"id":"physics1-circulation:e4","text":"Reynolds R = ρvr/η: aorta ≈ 4,500 (turbulent); medium vessels laminar.","topic":"Blood and flow laws","sec":1,"importance":"core","highYield":"insufficient-source"},{"id":"physics1-circulation:e5","text":"Bernoulli: P + ρgh + ½ρv² = const.","topic":"Blood and flow laws","sec":1,"importance":"core","highYield":"insufficient-source"},{"id":"physics1-circulation:e6","text":"Stenosis: v ↑, P ↓ → murmur, thrill. Aneurysm: v ↓, P ↑.","topic":"Blood and flow laws","sec":1,"importance":"core","highYield":"insufficient-source"},{"id":"physics1-circulation:e7","text":"Total section maximal in capillaries → lowest velocity.","topic":"Velocity, section and Laplace","sec":2,"importance":"core","highYield":"insufficient-source"},{"id":"physics1-circulation:e8","text":"Laplace: T = P·r; larger radius, more tension.","topic":"Velocity, section and Laplace","sec":2,"importance":"core","highYield":"insufficient-source"}],"vmap":{},"mlevel":{"nx5xgf":"a","1o8mo9e":"a","mb0yz7":"a","1p5e46p":"a","1rt2n4v":"a","19kqp6l":"a","1tlyzvm":"a","c35mpp":"a","1vcxcf2":"a","15enldy":"a"},"mapCounts":{"verified":0,"auto":10,"ambiguous":0,"missing":0},"mrules":[],"items":[],"experimental":[],"status":{},"difficulty":{},"expl":{"physics1-circulation:e0":{"s":0,"u":["Circulation: heart (pump), blood (fluid), vessels (closed conduits).","The circulation is a closed circuit: a pump (heart), a fluid (blood) and conduits (vessels).","The heart is a double pump : the right heart drives the pulmonary circulation (right atrium → right ventricle → pulmonary artery → lungs), the left heart the systemic circulation (pulmonary veins → left atrium → left ventricle → aorta → organs), separated by the septa and connected by valves."],"dp":[]},"physics1-circulation:e1":{"s":0,"u":["Right heart: pulmonary circulation; left heart: systemic.","The heart is a double pump : the right heart drives the pulmonary circulation (right atrium → right ventricle → pulmonary artery → lungs), the left heart the systemic circulation (pulmonary veins → left atrium → left ventricle → aorta → organs), separated by the septa and connected by valves.","The circulation is a closed circuit: a pump (heart), a fluid (blood) and conduits (vessels)."],"dp":[]},"physics1-circulation:e2":{"s":1,"u":["Blood is non-Newtonian.","Blood is a suspension of cells in plasma and a non-Newtonian fluid whose viscosity rises in small vessels (reversible red-cell aggregation)."],"dp":[]},"physics1-circulation:e3":{"s":1,"u":["Poiseuille: Q = πr⁴ΔP/(8ηL); ↑ viscosity → ↑ pressure (hypertension).","A sustained rise in viscosity ( polycythaemia ) tends to lower flow; to keep flow constant, pressure rises: hypertension .","Poiseuille's law (laminar flow): Q = πr⁴ΔP/(8ηL) : resistance is proportional to viscosity and length and inversely to r⁴."],"dp":[]},"physics1-circulation:e4":{"s":1,"u":["Reynolds R = ρvr/η: aorta ≈ 4,500 (turbulent); medium vessels laminar.","Flow regimes : Reynolds number R = ρvr/η : in large vessels velocity is high and flow turbulent (aorta R ≈ 4,500); in medium vessels flow is laminar , with a plasma layer at the wall and cells centrally; in capillaries red cells pass in single file ."],"dp":[{"h":"Why a narrowed artery makes a noise","t":"Blood must speed up to pass a stenosis, and by Bernoulli its pressure drops. The fast jet raises the Reynolds number above the laminar limit, so flow becomes turbulent downstream. Turbulence vibrates the vessel wall, which a stethoscope hears as a murmur or bruit and a hand feels as a thrill. Source: the lecture's Bernoulli and Reynolds slides."}]},"physics1-circulation:e5":{"s":1,"u":["Bernoulli: P + ρgh + ½ρv² = const.","Bernoulli (energy conservation): P + ρgh + ½ρv² = constant ."],"dp":[]},"physics1-circulation:e6":{"s":1,"u":["Stenosis: v ↑, P ↓ → murmur, thrill. Aneurysm: v ↓, P ↑.","In a stenosis , velocity rises and pressure falls, causing turbulence heard as a murmur and felt as a thrill ; in an aneurysm , velocity falls and pressure rises."],"dp":[]},"physics1-circulation:e7":{"s":2,"u":["Total section maximal in capillaries → lowest velocity.","The total cross-sectional area increases from the aorta to the capillaries (maximal) and falls again toward the venae cavae; because flow = area × velocity ( Q = S·v ), velocity is lowest in the capillaries , favouring exchanges, then rises again in veins."],"dp":[]},"physics1-circulation:e8":{"s":2,"u":["Laplace: T = P·r; larger radius, more tension.","Laplace's law : the wall tension T = P·r (for a cylinder); for a given pressure, larger vessels bear more tension, which is why a dilated segment (aneurysm) tends to enlarge further and can rupture."],"dp":[]}},"meta":{"nx5xgf":{"a":"recall","vg":"physics1-circulation:e1/recall/1"},"1o8mo9e":{"a":"recall","vg":"physics1-circulation:e2/recall/1"},"mb0yz7":{"a":"recall","vg":"physics1-circulation:e3/recall/1"},"1p5e46p":{"a":"relationship","vg":"physics1-circulation:e3/relationship/1"},"1rt2n4v":{"a":"recall","vg":"physics1-circulation:e4/recall/1"},"19kqp6l":{"a":"recall","vg":"physics1-circulation:e5/recall/1"},"1tlyzvm":{"a":"recall","vg":"physics1-circulation:e6/recall/1"},"c35mpp":{"a":"recall","vg":"physics1-circulation:e6/recall/1"},"1vcxcf2":{"a":"recall","vg":"physics1-circulation:e7/recall/1"},"15enldy":{"a":"recall","vg":"physics1-circulation:e8/recall/1"}},"explRev":"acaa5a30e407"};
